            <div xml:id="d356">

                <pb facs="0535" n="441" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg441"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.512/3116: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-02-16T09:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 16,
                                1924—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>82. Following from American consul at Guadalajara: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“February 14, 5 p.m. State authorities have issued a decree requiring the
                            payment of taxes December, February inclusive, which the revolutionary
                            government exacted while in power. What shall I advise American citizens
                            as to repayment of these?”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
